  "label": "the speaker's self-deprecating reaction is mapped onto the quokka",
  "description": "The text describes the speaker's own reaction to the situation ('i was like, \"you're going to be 14 in a couple of years anyway, what's the rush?\"'), which is a self-deprecating comment. The quokka, with its innocent, smiling expression, visually represents this self-deprecating, slightly absurd, or 'cute' reaction to the bizarre scenario. The mapping is based on the juxtaposition of the quokka's wholesome appearance with the speaker's self-mocking tone.",
